# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Voxelforge .gitignore
# Keep: source (Rust crates, scripts, maps, docs), Cargo.lock, the
# curated golden refs in docs/assets/, and the hero-golden-* targets.
# Drop:  Rust build output, compiled binaries, and the hundreds of
#        experimental render/log artifacts the look passes left behind.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Rust / build artifacts ───────────────────────────────────
/target
**/target/
/dist
*.exe
*.pdb
# Cargo.lock is intentionally committed (binary crate → reproducible builds).

# ── Editor / OS / GPU cache junk ─────────────────────────────
*.bak-*
NVIDIA Corporation/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/

# ── Build & run logs (experimental cruft) ────────────────────
*.log
*.err
*.out
*.done
*.meta
*.nohup
bench-out.txt
logs_*.txt
# stray build-output notes dropped inside the client crate
client/build_*.txt

# ── Render outputs / experimental beauty-shot iterations ─────
# The look passes produced ~220 throwaway PNGs at the repo root.
# Ignore every top-level PNG, then re-include only the golden refs
# the acceptance workflow compares against. (docs/assets/*.png are
# in a subdirectory and are never matched by this root-only rule.)
/*.png
!/hero-golden-a.png
!/hero-golden-b.png
!/hero-golden-c.png

# ── Browser console dumps (manual wasm smoke-test artifacts) ─
# e.g. docs/assets/wasm-first-frame.png.console.txt — raw devtools
# console dumps saved alongside a screenshot; contain local paths /
# dev-server URLs and shouldn't be committed as source.
*.console.txt

# ── Godot prototype editor cache (unrelated to the Bevy client) ─
# godot/project.godot, scenes/, scripts/*.gd ARE real source and stay
# tracked — only the editor's own generated cache is junk.
godot/.godot/

# ── Editor runtime config (generated on first run, see editor_config.rs) ─
/editor_config.json

# ── Side-lane build dirs & throwaway probes ──────────────────
# `target-combat/` is a 3.2 GB CARGO_TARGET_DIR used by the combat lane so
# it never fights the main build's lock; `**/target/` above misses the name.
# `target-review/` is the same pattern for the review lane's own CARGO_TARGET_DIR.
/target-combat/
/target-review/
# Same pattern, one dir per lane so the lanes never fight each other's build
# lock. Together these are ~15 GB — every one of them must stay untracked.
/target-anim/
/target-audio/
/target-feel/
/target-hole/
/target-int/
/target-look/
/target-poppy/
/target-quest/
/target-vfx/
# Three new side-lane build dirs (Shiba / Rose / Sun — one target-dir per lane).
/target-shiba/
/target-rose/
/target-sun/
**/__pycache__/
# One-off rustc/cl.exe toolchain probes from the Windows link-error hunt.
/_check_rustc_cl.ps1
/_parse_cl.ps1
# editor_config.json is generated on first run — the root rule missed the
# copy the client writes next to its own crate.
client/editor_config.json

# ── Combat-lane proof evidence ───────────────────────────────
# `_combat_proof/` holds the team's build/run logs for prove_combat.sh. The
# logs themselves already match `*.log`, but the folder also collects one-off
# .patch snapshots — ignore the whole directory rather than deleting the
# evidence. Keep the files on disk; just don't track them.
/_combat_proof/
/_poppy_proof/
# Same for the quest lane's evidence + its one-line verdict file, and the
# `logs-*.txt` run dumps (the rule above only catches `logs_*.txt`).
/_quest_proof/
/_combat_proof_result.txt
logs-*.txt

# ── Build scratch & proof temp files ──────────────────────────
# PID files, proof-poll dumps, and one-shot check outputs that accumulate
# at the repo root during integration passes.  Keep them on disk (they are
# always regenerated); just don't track them.
_*.pid
_*.txt
_*.json
# Log-rotation suffixes (e.g. _dp_rebuild.log.1) — `*.log` alone misses these.
*.log.*
# Test recordings from clip harness dry-runs.
/_ddagrab_test.mp4
# Combat-lane recording scratch (raw MKV captures + review stills from
# record_combat_clip.ps1).
/_combat_recordings/
# Elden Ring reference data — imported weapon/animation dumps for research,
# never committed as source.
/er-tmp/
# Yamamoto integration gate scripts — regenerated per integration pass.
/_yama_*.sh

# Ship output directory (packaged EXE + assets — generated, ~80 MB).
/_ship/

# Wait-poller scripts (bare while/sleep loops that only make sense inside
# a live agent session — never committed as source).
/scripts/_*.sh

# ── Gate-3 shoot logs (generated per run, ~dozens of *.log + *.txt) ──
/_gate3_logs/

# Rose lane probe script (one-shot rustc/cl.exe toolchain check)
/scripts/_rose_probe_build.cmd

# Quarantine: orphaned external-crate files pending owner identification
/_quarantine_steamworks/

# One-shot review scripts (Python / PowerShell) — same convention as scripts/_*.sh
# `_[!_]*.py` (not `_*.py`) so it doesn't also swallow dunder package files
# like scripts/__init__.py / scripts/__main__.py.
/scripts/_[!_]*.py
/scripts/_*.ps1

# Steam capsule review proof images (Flamingo, 2026-08-01)
/docs/assets/steam/review/

# ── Per-lane shoot/sweep scratch dirs (2026-08-01) ───────────
# One dir per lane, same rationale as the `target-<lane>/` block above: they
# hold the PNG + .log evidence a sweep produced (e.g. `_poppy_colour_sweep/`
# is 32 frames + logs behind the magenta fix). Keep the evidence on disk —
# it is what a re-review reads — just never track ~30 MB of throwaway renders.
/_poppy_*/
/_rose_*/
# Kevin's CARGO_TARGET_DIR — the `target-<lane>` convention above missed the name.
/target-kevin/

# ── Blanket catch-alls (2026-08-05) ──────────────────────────
# The per-lane entries above are added one name at a time and keep missing
# new lanes (target-flamingo/, target-monanisa/ both leaked in as untracked
# before this rule existed). Blanket rules so no lane's scratch — any
# extension, any depth — needs its own line ever again. Evidence stays on
# disk; it's just never tracked. Do NOT delete anyone else's files under
# these patterns — ignoring is not deleting.
target-*/
_*/
# `_[!_]*.py` (not `_*.py`) so a python package's __init__.py/__main__.py
# under scripts/ (or anywhere) never gets silently ignored.
_[!_]*.py
_*.sh
_*.ps1
_*.marker
_*.patch

# ── Shipped grading infrastructure that lives under a `_` name ────────────
# These blanket rules mean "scratch", and they were right to — but a TRACKED
# script must never depend on a file the repo refuses to carry. That already
# happened once: scripts/grade_gate.py and grade_axes.py imported a guard module
# named `_nohud2_guard.py`, which `_[!_]*.py` swallowed, so a fresh clone would
# have had both graders die on ModuleNotFoundError before printing anything.
# The guard itself was fixed by RENAMING it (scripts/nohud2_guard.py) — the
# honest fix, because it was never scratch.
#
# `_flamingo_dehud2.py` is the other half of that chain: it is the tool the
# guard's refusal message tells you to run, and docs/look-acceptance-rubric.md
# (tracked) names it as the de-HUD step. It keeps its `_` name only because ~8
# scripts across three lanes already call it by that path; renaming it mid-flight
# would break other agents' running chains. So it is un-ignored in place.
#
# Add to this list only when a TRACKED file requires the path.
# tests/test_nohud2_guard.py fails if either of these stops being tracked.
!scripts/_flamingo_dehud2.py
#
# The regrade shotset pair (2026-08-07). docs/note-poppy-shotset-harness-2026-08-07.md
# gives `powershell -File scripts/_poppy_shotset.ps1` as the capture step, and
# docs/note-poppy-regrade-results-2026-08-07.md names the sheet script as the site of a
# fix it describes — two tracked docs depending on two files `_[!_]*.py` and `_*.ps1`
# swallowed. Un-ignored in place rather than renamed: the ps1 is invoked by name from
# both docs and from REGRADE.cmd on disk, and the `_` prefix pairs it with the
# `_poppy_shotset/` output dir it writes.
!scripts/_poppy_shotset.ps1
!scripts/_poppy_shotset_sheet.py
#
# The EV-ladder harness (2026-08-07). Same reasoning one step further: the ev100
# value in client/src/look.rs is justified IN ITS OWN COMMENT by numbers these two
# produced, so a reader who wants to re-derive that constant needs the tools, not
# just the result. `_grade_*.py` is a pattern rather than one path because the
# grader-side scripts are added one per axis-investigation and each new one was
# silently dropped by `_[!_]*.py` the same way.
!scripts/_grade_*.py
!scripts/_flamingo_ev_ladder.ps1

# ── Lane shoot/grade/capture tooling under `_` names (Director 2026-08-08) ──
# The `_[!_]*.py` / `_*.sh` / `_*.ps1` blanket rules above were right for OUTPUT
# scratch, but they also swallowed the TOOLING each lane wrote under a `_` prefix
# (shoot/grade/capture/probe/sheet/chain/sweep scripts). That is source, not
# scratch: the repo header lists `scripts` as kept source, and a disk failure
# takes every one of them with no recovery. Un-ignored in place, scoped to
# scripts/ and to code extensions only — root `_*.py` scratch and every `_*/`
# output dir (PNG/log/json/exe artifacts) stay ignored by the rules above, so
# nothing bulky reaches the repo through these three lines.
!scripts/_*.py
!scripts/_*.sh
!scripts/_*.ps1

# ── The regrade shotset's numeric evidence (2026-08-07) ───────────────────
# `_*/` above ignores the whole `_poppy_shotset/` output dir, and it should: that dir is
# 110 MB, most of it a copied 80 MB vfprobe.exe plus per-plate PNGs — artifacts, not
# source. But docs/note-poppy-regrade-results-2026-08-07.md (tracked) reports gate
# numbers and says "see regrade_table.txt for the full grid", so those three small text
# artifacts have to be carryable or the note cites nothing.
# Git cannot re-include a file inside an excluded directory, so the dir is un-ignored and
# its contents immediately re-ignored — allowlist, not blocklist. Adding a PNG or an exe
# to that dir still cannot reach the repo. Add a line here only for a file a TRACKED doc
# reads, and only if it is small and textual.
!/_poppy_shotset/
/_poppy_shotset/*
!/_poppy_shotset/regrade.json
!/_poppy_shotset/regrade_table.txt
!/_poppy_shotset/regrade_gates_crosscheck.txt

# ── The EV-ladder's numeric evidence (2026-08-07) ─────────────────────────
# Same allowlist shape, same reason: client/src/look.rs quotes this table inline to
# justify ev100 = 10.3, so the table has to be carryable or the constant cites a file
# a fresh clone does not have. Text only — `_flamingo_ev/` also holds ~40 MB of plate
# PNGs and a copied 80 MB probe exe, which stay out. The contact sheet that IS worth
# keeping was copied into docs/assets/ instead, where PNGs are tracked on purpose.
!/_flamingo_ev/
/_flamingo_ev/*
!/_flamingo_ev/LADDER.txt

# ── The concept-reference metrics every character grade compares against (2026-08-14) ─
# `_*/` ignores /_fl_char/, and for almost everything in it that is right: the dir holds
# an 80 MB vfchar.exe and ~5 MB of plate PNGs. But `ref-*.json` is the CONCEPT side of
# every character grade — the numbers a render is scored against. Nine tracked files
# already name `_fl_char/ref-auren-hero.json`, including three VERDICT docs and the
# A6.2' command block in docs/look-acceptance-rubric.md, so without these a fresh clone
# cannot run the gate the rubric specifies. Exactly the failure the `_nohud2_guard.py`
# block above describes, caught before it shipped rather than after.
# Same allowlist shape: un-ignore the dir, re-ignore its contents, name only the small
# text files. ~2 KB total — the exe and the PNGs still cannot reach the repo.
!/_fl_char/
/_fl_char/*
!/_fl_char/ref-*.json

# ── One-shot artifacts (2026-08-06 Kevin cleanup) ──
# One-shot rebuild script with a hardcoded local path.
/scripts/tests/step2_rebuild_audio.ps1

# ── Runtime state the game/harness writes on every run (2026-08-11) ──
# Not source: exit-code stubs from detached builds, the play-proof status file,
# the quest autosave, and the per-machine settings/editor config the running
# client rewrites. They churn on every launch and mean nothing to a fresh clone.
*.exitcode
/_shino_proof.status
/quest_save.json
/client/src/settings.json
/client/src/editor_config.json

# ── Worktree rescue backup (2026-08-14) ─────────────────────────────────
# `_*/` and `_*.patch` above are right for scratch, but this folder is the
# committed safety net for four live worktrees' uncommitted diffs (plus one
# worktree's untracked texture atlas) that must survive an accidental
# `git worktree remove`. Un-ignored in place so the backup actually tracks —
# the `_` names pair each .patch with its source worktree.
!docs/evidence/worktree-rescue-2026-08-14/_*.patch
!docs/evidence/worktree-rescue-2026-08-14/_vf_poppy_head_untracked/
!docs/evidence/worktree-rescue-2026-08-14/_vf_poppy_head_untracked/**

# ── Flamingo atmos-lane rescue backup (2026-08-14) ──────────────────────
# Same shape as the worktree-rescue block above: a safety copy of Flamingo's
# atmosphere-lane script trio plus the client/src/look.rs diff they back up,
# saved under docs/rescue/ before a risky worktree operation. `_*.sh` /
# `_[!_]*.py` above would silently drop the two scripts inside; allowlisted
# so the backup actually carries what it claims to.
!docs/rescue/_*.sh
!docs/rescue/_*.py

# ── One-shot build-launcher batch files with a hardcoded local absolute
# path (same reasoning as scripts/tests/step2_rebuild_audio.ps1 above) —
# never portable, always regenerated per machine/session.
/_shino_build_quest.cmd
